        let z = make_zip_archive(&[(b"iter.bin\0", &data)], 6);
        let path = format!("{}/zip_iter_extract.perf.bin", dir);
        fs::write(&path, &z).unwrap();
        lines.push(format!("perf zip_iter_extract {}", path));
    }

    {
        let buf = make_pattern_buf(1024, 0x77);
        let path = format!("{}/zip_file_ops.perf.bin", dir);
        fs::write(&path, &buf).unwrap();
        lines.push(format!("perf zip_file_ops {}", path));
    }

    lines
}
```

Looking at the error, the double free occurs in `op_zip_extended`. The issue is in the cleanup logic: when `mz_zip_writer_init_from_reader_v2` succeeds, the writer takes ownership of the archive buffer. After `mz_zip_writer_end`, the buffer has already been freed by the writer. But then we call `mz_free(archive_buf)` again at the end, causing a double free.

Similarly, when `mz_zip_writer_init_from_reader_v2` fails, we call `mz_zip_reader_end(pz_r)` which may also free the buffer, and then we free it again.

The fix: track whether the archive buffer has been consumed by the reader/writer and skip the manual `mz_free` in that case.

